{"id":"6b4ef994ff61ac47","group":"27","path":"27/27-thm-monodual.md","title":"Dual preserves positivity","display":"thm-monodual — Dual preserves positivity","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications","book_abbrev":"27","label":"27-thm-monodual","aliases":["27-thm-monodual"],"display":"thm-monodual — Dual preserves positivity","depends_on":["[[27-df-monotone]]","[[27-df-dual]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Boolean Functions: Theory, Algorithms, and Applications"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"27"},{"key":"label","html":"27-thm-monodual"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>27-thm-monodual</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-monodual — Dual preserves positivity"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"640eb8f2fbffd9d9\" href=\"?note=640eb8f2fbffd9d9\" title=\"27-df-monotone\">27-df-monotone</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"b491e41297256b44\" href=\"?note=b491e41297256b44\" title=\"27-df-dual\">27-df-dual</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\\in\\mathbb N\">\\(n\\in\\mathbb N\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"[n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}\">\\([n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}\\)</span>; <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}\">\\(\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}\">\\(\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}\\)</span>, as in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5d10aed668d85817\" href=\"?note=5d10aed668d85817\" title=\"27-df-boolfunc\">27-df-boolfunc</a>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Dual}_n\">\\(\\mathrm{Dual}_n\\)</span> are defined in <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"640eb8f2fbffd9d9\" href=\"?note=640eb8f2fbffd9d9\" title=\"27-df-monotone\">27-df-monotone</a> and <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"b491e41297256b44\" href=\"?note=b491e41297256b44\" title=\"27-df-dual\">27-df-dual</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\forall f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\;\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\\mathrm{Dual}_n(f)\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\right).\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\forall f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\;\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\\mathrm{Dual}_n(f)\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\right).\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>来源：Crama–Hammer (2011), §4.2.1, Theorem 4.17，印刷页 177，PDF 第 201 页（从 1 计数）。 已核对陈述；直接证明由输入取补逆序、输出取补再逆序及对偶的 involution 得出。</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"27-df-monotone","status":"resolved","id":"640eb8f2fbffd9d9","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-monotone]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-dual","status":"resolved","id":"b491e41297256b44","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[27-df-dual]]","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-boolfunc","status":"resolved","id":"5d10aed668d85817","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$n\\in\\mathbb N$, $[n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}$; $\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}$ and $\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}$, as in [[27-df-boolfunc]].","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-monotone","status":"resolved","id":"640eb8f2fbffd9d9","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Monotone}_n$ and $\\mathrm{Dual}_n$ are defined in [[27-df-monotone]] and [[27-df-dual]].","embed":false},{"target":"27-df-dual","status":"resolved","id":"b491e41297256b44","anchor":"ref-5","targetAnchor":"","location":"正文","heading":"[Hypothesis]","excerpt":"$\\mathrm{Monotone}_n$ and $\\mathrm{Dual}_n$ are defined in [[27-df-monotone]] and [[27-df-dual]].","embed":false}],"attachments":[],"math":[{"tex":"n\\in\\mathbb N","display":false},{"tex":"[n]=\\{1,\\ldots,n\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathbb B=\\{0,1\\}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n=\\mathbb B^{\\mathbb B^n}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Monotone}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Dual}_n","display":false},{"tex":"\\forall f\\in\\mathrm{BoolFunc}_n\\;\\left(f\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\;\\leftrightarrow\\;\\mathrm{Dual}_n(f)\\in\\mathrm{Monotone}_n\\right).","display":true}],"bytes":952,"backlinks":[{"id":"5244dbb38da17b8a","anchor":"ref-471","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[27-thm-monodual|thm-monodual — Dual preserves positivity]]"}],"outgoing":["640eb8f2fbffd9d9","b491e41297256b44","5d10aed668d85817"]}